2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-1147) 'What EditScore costs and returns
 # uuid: ae8ab222-96b0-5cf0-8d9d-28b2c9f45fa1
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:attest-in:none
 RFD:Published  1 RFD
 Serials:Weftspun

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-1147) 'the scorer shared by all four loops
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-1147) '`fourloops-plan.exs`
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1147) 'The scorer shared by all four loops has one document for its cost and its score.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1147) 'EditScore's measurements were written into RFD66606-1144, so a reader of loop 3 had to know to look in loop 2 for what the scorer costs.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1147) 'Cite this RFD, and not RFD66606-1144, when a loop needs the scorer's peak memory or its overall score.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1147) 'What EditScore costs and returns
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1147) 'Measured on the desk described in `logbook-fourloops-first-runs.md`, which holds the apparatus these figures come from. The entry says how the runs were made and this file says what they returned; re-running them needs the entry.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1147) 'Give the scorer its own RFD, and let the loops cite it.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1147) '`DETAILS.md` holds what it costs and what it returns: peak memory at 512 and at 1024 square, the overall score for an instruction the edit matched, and the two-axis spread behind that overall. Both `fourloops-plan.exs` and `fourloops-etnf.exs` name it as a source, so a quantity in either layer resolves against the scorer's own document.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1147) '**Its negative control makes the number a measurement.** A nonsense instruction returns 0.0 overall. A scorer that returns a middling figure for nonsense has not discriminated, and its score for a real edit would mean nothing.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1147) 'RFD66606-1143 through RFD66606-1146 are the four loops that score with it. RFD66606-1122 is the goal they serve.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1147) 'What it returns when the instruction matched
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1147) '| scale max | consistency | a second axis | overall |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1147) '| --------: | ----------: | ------------: | ------: |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-1147) '|      10.0 |         9.2 |           2.0 |    4.29 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-1147) 'The overall figure is 4.29 out of 10.0, and the spread behind it is the reason to carry both. Consistency scored 9.2 while the second axis scored 2.0, so a scorer reporting only the overall would say "middling" about a result that is excellent on one axis and poor on another. Which axis failed is the actionable half, and the overall alone discards it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-1147) '**The negative control.** A nonsense instruction returns 0.0 overall. That makes 4.29 a measurement rather than an impression: a scorer that cannot return 0.0 for nonsense is not discriminating, and every score it gives is consistent with it having read nothing. `editscoreNonsenseOverall = 0.0` in `fourloops-plan.exs` carries that control beside the quantity it validates.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-1147) 'What it costs
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1147) '| configuration  | peak       | seconds  |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1147) '| -------------- | ---------- | -------- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-1147) '| NF4, 512 x 512 | 6.7506 GiB | 28 to 36 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-1147) '| NF4, 1024 x 1024 | 8.6 GiB  |          |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-1147) '6.7506 GiB is measured; the plan rounds it to 6.75 in `editscorePeakGib512`, and carries 8.6 as `editscorePeakGib1024`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-1147) 'The seconds are a range rather than a median, and deliberately. The run-to-run spread at 512 is wider than the gap between the two OmniGen2 precisions RFD66606-1144 reports, so a single figure would imply a resolution these runs do not support.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-1147) 'Where the apparatus lives
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1147) '`logbook-fourloops-first-runs.md` keeps the apparatus, and this RFD keeps the result. The entry says how the runs were made, which is what lets somebody make them again.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-1147) 'Why the measurements moved
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-1147) 'Its measurements were written into RFD66606-1144 because loop 2 is the smallest loop that exercises it. That put a figure belonging to four loops inside the document for one of them.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-1147) 'Why this lives in its own document
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-1147) 'Every loop in `fourloops-plan.exs` names EditScore as its `score` stage, and loop 1 pairs it with the Referee because an image scorer and a body scorer answer different questions. A figure that four loops depend on belongs beside none of them in particular.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-1147) 'It was in RFD66606-1144 first, on the reasoning that loop 2 is the smallest loop exercising the scorer and so its numbers were the plan's. That reasoning holds for OmniGen2, which loops 2 and 3 use and loops 1 and 4 do not. It does not hold for a stage all four share.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-1147) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-1147) 'EditScore is the `score` stage of every loop in `fourloops-plan.exs`. Loops 1 through 4 each name it, and loop 1 pairs it with the Referee.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1147  1 LINE
 Text:Written
